WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.482 --> 00:00:14.465
Mr. Jaggers came to Miss Havisham's to dine that night.

2
00:00:15.465 --> 00:00:17.346
Miss Havisham did not join us, and Mr.

3
00:00:17.366 --> 00:00:20.627
Jaggers explained that she never let anyone see her eat or drink.

4
00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:22.948
"She wanders during the night.

5
00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:25.309
That's when she gets something to eat."

6
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.391
Later we played cards with Estella and Miss Havisham, and it was agreed that I would meet Estella's

7
00:00:30.451 --> 00:00:31.712
coach when she came to London.

8
00:00:32.672 --> 00:00:33.493
That night Mr.

9
00:00:33.513 --> 00:00:35.415
Jaggers and I stayed at the Blue Boar Inn.

10
00:00:36.395 --> 00:00:40.519
I lay awake, thinking of Estella and wondering when she would begin to be interested in me.

11
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.802
The next morning at breakfast I resolved to tell Mr.

12
00:00:43.842 --> 00:00:47.826
Jaggers that I didn't think Orlick was the right sort of person to fill a position of trust

13
00:00:47.966 --> 00:00:48.766
at Miss Havisham's.

14
00:00:48.786 --> 00:00:51.269
"Very good, Pip," said Mr.

15
00:00:51.289 --> 00:00:52.470
Jaggers when I had finished.

16
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.032
"I'll go back today and pay him off."

17
00:00:56.053 --> 00:00:57.014
I was alarmed that Mr.

18
00:00:57.054 --> 00:00:59.356
Jaggers was going to dismiss Orlick so quickly.

19
00:01:00.872 --> 00:01:03.253
I even hinted that Orlick might be difficult to deal with.

20
00:01:03.273 --> 00:01:06.093
"Oh no, he won't," said Mr.

21
00:01:06.134 --> 00:01:08.954
Jaggers. "I'd like to see him argue with me."

22
00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:12.175
Later that day we traveled back to London together.

23
00:01:13.195 --> 00:01:16.996
As soon as I arrived in the city, I sent a codfish and a barrel of oysters to

24
00:01:17.057 --> 00:01:19.197
Joe to apologize for not visiting him.

25
00:01:20.197 --> 00:01:22.918
At Barnard's Inn I found Herbert having a cold supper.

26
00:01:23.918 --> 00:01:27.799
He was delighted to welcome me back, and after eating we sat in front of the fire and

27
00:01:27.859 --> 00:01:30.993
talked. "Herbert, I have something to tell you.

28
00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:34.275
I love—adore—Estella."

29
00:01:35.276 --> 00:01:39.119
Instead of being surprised, Herbert said, "Of course I know that."

30
00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:41.040
"How do you know that?

31
00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:42.781
I never told you."

32
00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.863
"You didn't have to tell me.

33
00:01:45.723 --> 00:01:47.465
You've adored her ever since I've known you.

34
00:01:48.365 --> 00:01:50.547
But now I must say something disagreeable to you.

35
00:01:51.948 --> 00:01:53.209
Think of how she was brought up.

36
00:01:54.229 --> 00:01:55.210
Think of Miss Havisham.

37
00:01:56.091 --> 00:01:57.592
Think of how Estella is herself.

38
00:01:58.508 --> 00:01:59.849
This may all lead to misery.

39
00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:01.611
Can't you forget her?"

40
00:02:01.631 --> 00:02:04.273
"No! It's impossible!"

41
00:02:04.293 --> 00:02:06.174
"You can't try?"

42
00:02:06.194 --> 00:02:10.498
"No!" An uncomfortable silence fell between us.

43
00:02:11.559 --> 00:02:16.323
Herbert got up and busied himself with tidying the room, putting chairs back where they belonged and straightening

44
00:02:16.383 --> 00:02:16.863
up books.

45
00:02:18.024 --> 00:02:20.166
Finally he came back and sat down near the fire.

46
00:02:20.186 --> 00:02:22.748
"Now I must tell you something.

47
00:02:23.589 --> 00:02:25.350
I am engaged, but it's a secret."

48
00:02:26.351 --> 00:02:27.292
"May I ask her name?"

49
00:02:28.256 --> 00:02:30.417
"Clara." "Does she live in London?"

50
00:02:30.437 --> 00:02:33.378
"Yes, she lives with her father, an invalid.

51
00:02:34.279 --> 00:02:38.201
I've never seen him because he keeps to his room upstairs, but I've heard him constantly.

52
00:02:39.021 --> 00:02:42.102
He roars and he pounds on the floor with some frightful instrument."

53
00:02:42.122 --> 00:02:44.784
"Don't you expect to see him?"

54
00:02:44.804 --> 00:02:47.765
"Oh yes, I constantly expect to see him.

55
00:02:48.725 --> 00:02:51.747
I never hear him without expecting him to come tumbling through the ceiling."

56
00:02:52.687 --> 00:02:53.928
Herbert laughed at his joke.

57
00:02:54.996 --> 00:02:58.797
He told me that the moment he made enough money, it was his intention to marry this young

58
00:02:58.837 --> 00:03:03.498
lady. As we stared at the fire, I thought about how difficult it was to make enough money.

59
00:03:04.479 --> 00:03:08.580
The days passed, and one day when I was busy with my studies, I received a note in

60
00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.000
the mail.

61
00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.501
Although I had never seen the handwriting before, I knew it was from Estella.

62
00:03:14.521 --> 00:03:18.222
She said that she would be arriving in London the day after tomorrow and asked me to meet

63
00:03:18.262 --> 00:03:18.763
her coach!

64
00:03:19.843 --> 00:03:23.744
If there had been time, I probably would have ordered several suits of clothes for this occasion.

65
00:03:24.768 --> 00:03:27.590
But since there wasn't time, I had to be content with what I owned.

66
00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:32.292
My appetite vanished and I knew no peace until the day arrived.

67
00:03:33.293 --> 00:03:36.194
In her traveling dress, Estella seemed more beautiful than ever.

68
00:03:37.235 --> 00:03:39.636
Her manner was more charming toward me than ever before.

69
00:03:40.537 --> 00:03:43.098
We stood near the inn while she pointed out her luggage to me.

70
00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:47.340
When it was all collected, I remembered that I knew nothing of her destination.

71
00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.822
"I'm traveling ten miles to Richmond," she said.

72
00:03:50.842 --> 00:03:53.524
"I am to have a carriage and you are to take me.

73
00:03:54.432 --> 00:03:57.175
This is my purse and you are to pay my expenses from it."

74
00:03:58.216 --> 00:03:59.577
I hesitated to take her purse.

75
00:03:59.597 --> 00:04:01.899
"Oh, you must take the purse!"

76
00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.040
she insisted.

77
00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:06.984
"We have no choice, you and I, but to obey our instructions.

78
00:04:07.985 --> 00:04:10.127
We are not free to follow our own minds."

79
00:04:11.148 --> 00:04:14.171
As she looked at me, I hoped there was some hidden meaning in her words.

80
00:04:14.191 --> 00:04:17.134
"A carriage will have to be sent for, Estella.

81
00:04:17.895 --> 00:04:18.896
Will you stay here a little?"

82
00:04:20.276 --> 00:04:23.819
"Yes, I am to stay here, and I am to drink some tea, and you are to take

83
00:04:23.859 --> 00:04:24.400
care of me."

84
00:04:25.281 --> 00:04:29.124
She put her arm through mine as if that were part of the instructions too, and we went

85
00:04:29.164 --> 00:04:30.285
into the inn for some tea.

86
00:04:30.305 --> 00:04:32.367
"Where are you going in Richmond?"

87
00:04:33.207 --> 00:04:34.789
I asked when we were seated at a table.

88
00:04:34.809 --> 00:04:39.153
"I'm going to live at great expense with a lady who has the power to take me around

89
00:04:39.313 --> 00:04:40.914
and introduce me to a lot of people.

90
00:04:41.835 --> 00:04:43.156
How do you enjoy living with Mr.

91
00:04:43.196 --> 00:04:50.073
Pocket?" "I live quite pleasantly there, at least I hesitated, at least as pleasantly as I could anywhere

92
00:04:50.093 --> 00:04:50.713
away from you."

93
00:04:50.733 --> 00:04:54.394
"You silly boy," Estella said quite calmly.

94
00:04:54.414 --> 00:04:56.915
"How can you talk such nonsense?"

95
00:04:57.975 --> 00:05:00.736
And then she went on talking about Matthew Pocket and his family.

96
00:05:01.656 --> 00:05:05.877
Apparently there were others in the family who regularly gave Miss Havisham bad reports about me.

97
00:05:07.178 --> 00:05:10.939
But Estella said I should not worry because nothing could make Miss Havisham dislike me.

98
00:05:11.899 --> 00:05:15.340
Estella, in fact, was entertained by the efforts of these relatives to discredit me.

99
00:05:16.328 --> 00:05:18.910
She playfully gave me her hand and I put it to my lips.

100
00:05:19.951 --> 00:05:21.992
"You ridiculous boy," she said.

101
00:05:22.012 --> 00:05:24.834
"You should have asked before you touched my hand."

102
00:05:24.854 --> 00:05:26.775
"May I kiss your cheek?"

103
00:05:26.795 --> 00:05:28.336
"If you like."

104
00:05:29.317 --> 00:05:31.939
I leaned down, and her calm face was like a statue's.

105
00:05:31.959 --> 00:05:37.943
"Now," said Estella, gliding away the instant I kissed her cheek, "you are to take me to Richmond."

106
00:05:38.863 --> 00:05:40.885
We got into a carriage and began our journey.

107
00:05:41.765 --> 00:05:44.267
When we passed through Hammersmith, I showed her where Mr.

108
00:05:44.307 --> 00:05:45.288
Matthew Pocket lived.

109
00:05:46.376 --> 00:05:49.878
I said it wasn't far from Richmond and that I hoped I would see her sometimes.

110
00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.701
"Oh yes, you are to come when you think it's proper.

111
00:05:54.502 --> 00:05:56.243
You have already been mentioned to the family."

112
00:05:56.263 --> 00:06:01.106
"I'm surprised that Miss Havisham could part with you again so soon after your return from France."

113
00:06:02.187 --> 00:06:05.949
"It's part of her plans for me, Pip," said Estella, sighing as if she were tired.

114
00:06:05.969 --> 00:06:11.213
"I am to write to her constantly and see her regularly and report on how I'm doing."

115
00:06:12.193 --> 00:06:15.956
That was the first time she'd ever called me by my name, and I treasured it.

116
00:06:16.972 --> 00:06:19.253
We arrived at the house in Richmond all too soon.

117
00:06:20.154 --> 00:06:22.495
Two maids came fluttering out to receive Estella.

118
00:06:23.395 --> 00:06:25.096
The doorway soon absorbed her boxes.

119
00:06:26.096 --> 00:06:29.738
She gave me her hand and a smile and was then absorbed into the house too.

120
00:06:30.798 --> 00:06:33.980
After the door shut, I continued to stand there, looking at the house.

121
00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.602
I thought about how happy I would be if I lived there with her.

122
00:06:38.542 --> 00:06:40.323
Yet I knew I was never happy with her.

123
00:06:41.263 --> 00:06:42.484
I was always miserable.
